FACT second_tablets.the_third_forty_and_the_go(i_stood_on_the_mount) = ("I stood on the mount (10:10) — the third forty as a STRETCH: the second ascent's marker (1, 5, 29) to the timers' fire (1, 7, 10) = 40 on the clock (ER.ascent('forty'), NR.the_forty_days by CALL): the readback row VERBATIM in kind; 'stood' against 9:9's 'sat' (Megillah 21a:17)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:10 — "AND I STOOD ON THE MOUNT AS AT THE FIRST DAYS, FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" — "and I stood on the mount" [\'Deut 10:10\'] (the one seat; 9:9\'s "and I sat on the mount"); "as at the first days" [\'Deut 10:10\', \'Zech 8:11\']; the parser [40, 40]; the phrase\'s nine Bible seats [\'1Kgs 19:8\', \'Deut 10:10\', \'Deut 9:11\', \'Deut 9:18\', \'Deut 9:9\', \'Exod 24:18\', \'Exod 34:28\', \'Gen 7:12\', \'Gen 7:4\']; the shared run with 9:9 6, 9:11 6, 34:28 5, 24:18 5'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_erection (CALL) — ER.ascent(forty) = 9; cold_run_not_righteousness (CALL) — NR.the_forty_days(forty_days_forty_nights) = forty days and forty nights (9:9, 9:11, 9:18, 9:25) — the pa — the phrase at nine seats (the erection's count names 10:10 among Moses' ascents); 7b's four stretch rows (9:9, 9:11 the first forty; 9:18, 9:25 the second) — THE THIRD HERE"), ('MOVE', "cold_run_not_righteousness (CALL) — NR.the_forty_days(i_sat_on_the_mount) = I sat on the mount (9:9) — against 10:10's 'I stood': four readings (M — 'I SAT' (9:9) against 'I STOOD' (10:10) — Megillah 21a:17's four readings (stood to learn, sat to review; bowing; remaining; easy standing, difficult sitting)"), ('DATA', 'THE STRETCH ROW (T6) — from the marker at Exod 34:4 (M[\'second_ascent\'] = (1, 5, 29), day 894460) to the timers\' fire tablets_delivered and face_radiant at (1, 7, 10) (day 894500): 40 — DA4\'s third forty read back; the stretch\'s end a TIMER\'S FIRE, not a marker (the probe\'s resolver takes both — the design named the fire); Onkelos "ארבעין יממין וארבעין לילון" (forty days and forty nights)')])
FACT second_tablets.the_third_forty_and_the_go(the_second_ascents_date) = ("the second ascent's date — Seder Olam Rabbah 6:2: up the 29th of Av 'as at the first days', down the 10th of Tishri: the machine's (1, 5, 29) by subtraction from 10 Tishri IS the shelf's date — MATCH; 7b's OPEN row on the clock CLOSED (the 'first of Elul' not this shelf's text; item (iii) paid)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Exod 34:28 — "forty days and forty nights" — the parser [40, 40, 10]; the timers set on the second ascent\'s line fired at (1, 7, 10) = 10 Tishri (CAL_PARAMS second_tablets_given); the marker at 34:4 by subtraction (1, 5, 29); Av\'s days that year 30; 29 Av to 10 Tishri 40'), ('MOVE', 'Seder Olam Rabbah 6:2 (READ WHOLE at the docket — the export\'s chapters under its EMPTY key; 7b\'s "unreachable" the reader\'s index, not the export\'s) — THE ASCENTS\' DATES — up on the seventh day after the Ten Words, down on the seventeenth of Tammuz; up on the eighteenth of Tammuz, DOWN ON THE TWENTY-EIGHTH OF AV AND CARVED THE TABLETS; UP ON THE TWENTY-NINTH OF AV — \'as at the first days\' (the first and the third of favor, the middle of anger); down on the tenth of Tishri, the Day of Atonement: THE MACHINE\'S (1, 5, 29) IS THE SHELF\'S OWN DATE'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_not_righteousness (CALL) — NR.the_forty_days(the_second_forty) = the second forty (9:18, 9:25) — the morrow (1, 4, 18) to the second ascent (1, 5 — 7b's OPEN row on the clock — 'the machine's 29 Av by subtraction against the tradition's 1 Elul' — WRONGLY FRAMED at 7b as the tradition's: Seder Olam 6:2 itself says the twenty-ninth of Av; the row CLOSED by the docket (7b's owed item (iii) PAID; DB4 retyped from OPEN to MATCH)"), ('DATA', 'THE MATCH — the calendar\'s subtraction and the shelf\'s row agree by the row\'s own count: 29 Av + 40 = 10 Tishri (Av thirty days, Elul twenty-nine on the tape\'s calendar that year); the second forty (18 Tammuz to 28 Av) the shelf\'s, the machine\'s (1, 4, 18) → (1, 5, 29) the morrow to the second ascent — the two counts one day apart at the end (the "down and carved" day the shelf\'s own); a DATA row; the exam\'s person the one who dates the second ascent — the rule holds (Seder Olam\'s)')])
FACT second_tablets.the_third_forty_and_the_go(hearkened_that_time_also) = ("the LORD hearkened to me that time also (10:10) — 9:19's clause verbatim (the six tokens at the two seats alone): TURNED — Exodus 32:14's relenting told as hearkening, decree_relented's entry referenced again (NR.the_intercession by CALL); Onkelos 'accepted my prayer'", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:10 — "AND THE LORD HEARKENED TO ME THAT TIME ALSO" — the six-token clause at 10:10 and 9:19 ALONE [\'Deut 10:10\', \'Deut 9:19\'] [\'וישמע\', \'יהוה\', \'אלי\', \'גם\', \'בפעם\', \'ההוא\']; "that time" the noun\'s book seats [(\'Deut 1:11\', \'פעמים\'), (\'Deut 9:19\', \'בפעם\'), (\'Deut 10:10\', \'בפעם\'), (\'Deut 16:16\', \'פעמים\')]'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_not_righteousness (CALL) — NR.the_intercession(the_lord_hearkened) = the LORD hearkened to me (9:19) — 32:14's relenting told as hearkening (one token shared): — 9:19's row TURNED — Exodus 32:14's 'and the LORD relented' told as hearkening; decree_relented ONE on Israel the entry, no second write; here the doublet — 'also' the second time's own word"), ('MOVE', "Berakhot 32b:8 (credited — chapter 4's docket, reread at 7b) — the prolonger of prayer assured — 'the forty days and forty nights that I fell down' (9:25) with 'and the LORD hearkened to me that time also' (10:10): the measure of prayer's proof-text at this verse"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 10:10 (the hearkening) TURNED — the tape\'s moses_interceded (Exodus 32:11-14, plea relent) by kind and first verse; decree_relented\'s entry referenced a second time (9:19\'s doublet); Onkelos "וקביל יי צלותי" (and the LORD accepted my prayer) at 9:19 and 10:10')])
FACT second_tablets.the_third_forty_and_the_go(not_willing_to_destroy) = ("the LORD was not willing to destroy you (10:10) — the one seat of the clause; 4:31's 'He will not destroy you' the kin; a declaration after the hearkening, no write; Onkelos whole", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:10 — "THE LORD WAS NOT WILLING TO DESTROY YOU" — "the LORD was not willing" [\'Deut 10:10\'] (the one seat; the willing-lemma\'s Torah seats [\'Deut 1:26\', \'Deut 2:30\', \'Deut 10:10\', \'Deut 13:9\', \'Deut 23:6\', \'Deut 25:7\', \'Deut 29:19\', \'Exod 10:27\', \'Gen 24:5\', \'Gen 24:8\', \'Lev 26:21\'] — 1:26, 2:30, 13:9, 23:6, 25:7, 29:19 the book\'s); "to destroy you" [\'2Chr 25:16\', \'2Chr 35:21\', \'Deut 10:10\', \'Deut 4:31\'] (4:31\'s "He will not destroy you" the kin)'), ('DATA', 'Onkelos "לא צבא יי לחבלותך" (the LORD was not willing to destroy you) — the retelling\'s own clause after the hearkening; 4:31 "the merciful God … will not destroy you" (obey_horeb.the_exile_case by CALL at 7b) the kin forward; no write (a declaration)')])
FACT second_tablets.the_third_forty_and_the_go(arise_go) = ("arise, go (10:11) — Exodus 32:34's and 33:1's command told again (five tokens with 33:1), NO LINE on the tape for either speech: the hole named OUTSIDE the span (an Exodus 33 sitting's); the readback row VARIANT; 'which I swore' sworn_by_himself (Gen 22:16) by kind", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:11 — "AND THE LORD SAID TO ME: ARISE, GO ON THE JOURNEY BEFORE THE PEOPLE, that they may go in and possess the land which I swore to their fathers to give them" — the chapter\'s ONE divine frame [11]; "arise, go" [\'Deut 10:11\', \'Gen 28:2\', \'Num 22:20\'] (Genesis 28:2, Numbers 22:20 the others); "on the journey" the noun\'s Torah seats [(\'Deut 10:11\', \'למסע\'), (\'Exod 17:1\', \'למסעיהם\'), (\'Exod 40:36\', \'מסעיהם\')] (the one singular with the preposition); "which I swore to their fathers to give them" [\'Deut 10:11\']; the shared run with Exodus 33:1 5, 32:34 3, Deut 1:8 5'), ('DATA', 'THE HOLE NAMED OUTSIDE THE SPAN (decision 7) — Exodus 32:34 "go, lead the people to the place of which I have spoken" and 33:1 "go up from here, you and the people … to the land which I swore to Abraham, to Isaac and to Jacob" HAVE NO LINE on the tape (God\'s speeches dropped by the erection\'s register test; 7b\'s owed item (vii) named the crowns and the three requests as holes outside chapter 9\'s span): an Exodus 33 sitting\'s, if ever — NOT FILLED HERE; the readback row 10:11 VARIANT against the ink of 32:34 and 33:1 (five tokens with 33:1)'), ('DATA', '"which I swore to their fathers" — the tape\'s sworn_by_himself (Genesis 22:16-18, subject abraham) by kind and first verse; 7:8\'s and 9:5\'s form; Onkelos "קום זיל למטל קדם עמא" (arise, go to journey before the people)')])
