FACT firstfruits_ebal_curses.the_removal_and_the_confession(when_you_have_finished_tithing_in_the_third_year) = ("when you have finished tithing in the third year (26:12) — the removal at the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year, every tithe to its owner, the second tithe and the first fruits removed, the cooked dish the two Houses' arms; one tithe not two, the seventh year exempt (the Sifrei 302:1, 109:4-5; Maaser Sheni 5:6 in the spine's own Hebrew; food_tithe's the removal's date (14:28) — the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; the Sifrei 109:1-3 — I2 with 31:10): THE PARAMETER the_removal_date, the date the calendar's own key; the one who removes the tithes on that eve accepted, one tithe not two (14:28) — the poor man's tithe replaces the second in the third and the sixth year (the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5), the Levite never interrupted (KO.the_tithe by CALL): THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a STATUS on Israel at the chapter's own day; the readback row 14:28 SUPPLIED AS A LAW with its write and the seventh year by the cycle (14:28) — the third and the sixth work years, the seventh the sabbath of the land (YO.cycle by CALL; CA.sabbatical 'land released in year 7'; the Sifrei 109:4): the one who would tithe the seventh year's produce exempt by CALL): THE WRITES tithe_removal_commanded, a STATUS, and poor_tithe_owed REUSED — a second entry on Israel at the chapters' own day; the removal at Shavuot refused", ['tithe_removal_commanded', 'poor_tithe_owed'], [('INK', "Deut 26:12 — 'WHEN YOU HAVE FINISHED TITHING all the tithe of your yield IN THE THIRD YEAR, THE YEAR OF THE TITHE' — 'finished' the verse's own clock; 'the year of the tithe' one tithe; the tithe's two tokens starred by the store (the ten's homograph — the reading's parser ['לעשר*', 'מעשר*'])"), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 302:1 (read whole — the end-analogy with 31:10 and 15:1 weighed and REFUSED by the verse's own 'finished'; MISHNAH MAASER SHENI 5:6 CITED IN THE SPINE'S OWN HEBREW at 302:1 and 109:3, the exam row read whole); the Sifrei 109:4-5 (the seventh year exempt; one tithe not two); cold_run_food_tithe (CALL) — FT.the_third_year(the_removal_date) = the removal's date (14:28) — the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; the Sifrei 109:1-3 — I2 with 31:10): THE PARAMETER the_removal_date, the date the calendar's own key; the one who removes the tithes on that eve accepted, (one_tithe_not_two) = one tithe not two (14:28) — the poor man's tithe replaces the second in the third and the sixth year (the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5), the Levite never interrupted (KO.the_tithe by CALL): THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a STATUS on Israel at the chapter's own day; the readback row 14:28 SUPPLIED AS A LAW with its write, (the_seventh_year_by_the_cycle) = the seventh year by the cycle (14:28) — the third and the sixth work years, the seventh the sabbath of the land (YO.cycle by CALL; CA.sabbatical 'land released in year 7'; the Sifrei 109:4): the one who would tithe the seventh year's produce exempt — THE REMOVAL AT THE EVE OF THE LAST FESTIVAL DAY OF PASSOVER of the fourth and the seventh year (others: the first) — the terumah and the terumah of the tithe to their owners, the first tithe to its owner, the poor's tithe to its owner, the second tithe and the first fruits removed in every place; R. Shimon: the first fruits to the priests like terumah; the cooked dish — the House of Shammai removes, the House of Hillel as removed (Maaser Sheni 5:6 — the arms recorded); the poor man's tithe REPLACES the second in the third and the sixth year; the seventh year exempt"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE tithe_removal_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DL2) — and poor_tithe_owed REUSED at 26:12 (a second entry — 14:28's the first; the recon's 1 before, 2 after — REU