ng with TWO ARMS — 28:1-14 the blessing's, 28:15-68 the curse's: the two verses upheld by a condition as a STATE ROW (13b's form — 15:4 and 15:11 the precedent), the DATA row the_hearkening_state naming the twelve twins seat for seat (40:10-11); blessings_for_hearing REUSED — the conditional heaven entry's third seat, the fullest (7:12's and 15:5's before it)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE blessings_for_hearing REUSED at 28:1 (a third entry — the recon's 2 before, 3 after; REUSE_COUNTS 3); THE STATE ROW at 28:1 and 28:15 — the_hearkening_state a DATA row with two arms; the readback row 28:1 SUPPLIED with the line's five writes, state=True; the exam's person the people who hearken — the blessing's arm")])
