FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_release_at_the_years_end) = ("the release at the year's end (15:1) — 'end' is the year's end by I2 with 31:10 (the Sifrei 111:1; Rosh Hashanah 8b; Arakhin 28b:7): the release date a clock datum by CALL to the cycle (yovel.cycle(7) sabbath_of_the_land; 'no count' on the bare world): the creditor who collects in the seventh year's first month accepted — the loan released only at its end", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:1 — "AT THE END OF SEVEN YEARS you shall make a release" — the verse [\'מקץ\', \'שבע\', \'שנים\', \'תעשה\', \'שמטה\'], the parser\'s [7] [7]; "at the end of seven years" [\'Deut 15:1\', \'Deut 31:10\', \'Jer 34:14\'] (the assembly 31:10, Jeremiah 34:14 the run\'s case); the release noun\'s five tokens [\'שמטה\', \'השמטה\', \'שמטה\', \'השמטה\', \'השמטה\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 111:1 (read whole at the reading); Rosh Hashanah 8b:8-12, Arakhin 28b:7 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.cycle(7) = sabbath_of_the_land, YO.cycle(14) = sabbath_of_the_land; the running world's count on the bare world = no count — 'END' IS THE YEAR'S END, NOT ITS BEGINNING — 'end' is said here and 'end' is said at 31:10's assembly (I2, checked in MIDDOT.md): as there at its end, so here (111:1); Sheviit 10:1 the seventh year releases at its end; Rosh Hashanah 8b the first of Tishri the sabbatical's new year, Arakhin 28b:7 the release at the year's END against the jubilee's onset at its new year: THE RELEASE DATE A CLOCK DATUM — the last day of the year whose class is sabbath_of_the_land, read from the cycle by CALL, never a constant; the loan released ON THE ACT (Rosh Hashanah 9b:2-3 'even though they did not release' — the yovel engine's own routed_deut_15 cell)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE debt_release_owed — a STATUS on israel_people at the counter's day (40, 11, 1) (DG2, DG4): its value the_release_date (calendar_parameters.yaml — the end, the year, the onset, the territory); on the bare world before the entry the count not begun: 'no count'; the exam's person the creditor who collects in the seventh year's first month — the release not yet: accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_one_calendar) = ("the one calendar (15:1) — seven years for the whole world, never for each debtor: the two paradigms deadlocked and broken by 'seven years'/'seven years' (the Sifrei 111:3-7 — I2), R. Yose the Galilean's 'draws near' (111:8): the creditor whose own seven years ended in the world's third year accepted — his loan stands until the world's seventh", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:1 — "seven years" — the number verse [7]; the noun "release" [\'Deut 15:1\', \'Deut 15:2\', \'Deut 15:2\', \'Deut 15:9\', \'Deut 31:10\'] at 15:1, 15:2 twice, 15:9, 31:10 — every seat in this book; the shared run with 31:10 3 and with Jeremiah 34:14 3'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 111:3-8 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.jubilee() cycle_length = 49, jubilee_year = 50 — ONE CALENDAR FOR THE WHOLE WORLD, NEVER FOR EACH DEBTOR — the two paradigms deadlocked (111:3-6: the land's release for the whole world / the Hebrew slave's six years for each one; not dependent on the jubilee / practiced outside the Land) and broken by THE ANALOGY THE ROW NAMES IN THE HEBREW: 'seven years'/'seven years' (I2, checked in MIDDOT.md — 111:7): as the land's seven years are the world's, so the loan's; R. Yose the Galilean's proof from 15:9 'the year of release DRAWS NEAR' (111:8; 117:4) — if each his own, how does it draw near?; the debtor's own clock THE REFUTED ARM"), ('DATA', "the one calendar a DATA row (the_one_calendar — the two paradigms and the analogy; the refuted arm the debtor's own clock); the exam's person the creditor whose own seven years from his loan ended in the world's third year — his loan stands until the world's seventh: accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_onset) = ("the onset (15:1) — after the conquest and the division (the Sifrei 111:9-11; 41:3; Arakhin 32b:10 the count renewed at Ezra's return, 32b:15-18 the jubilee nullified in the exile and the fiftieth counted to order the sabbaticals): THE PARAMETER the_release_onset; 'no count' before the entry: the creditor in the wilderness exempt from the release", ['exempt'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:1 — "you shall make a release" — the verb [\'תעשה\'] (the noun\'s root at 15:2 "release, release" [\'השמטה\', \'שמטה\']); the wilderness never named in the chapter []'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 111:9-11 (read whole at the reading); 41:3 (reread whole); Arakhin 32b:10-18, Rosh Hashanah 9a:1 (read whole at the docket); the running world's count = no count — THE ONSET AFTER THE CONQUEST AND THE DIVISION — might the release have been practiced in the wilderness? (111:9) 'you shall make a release … release' — where you make the land's release you release the loan (111:10): after the fourteen years (41:3); THE COUNT RENEWED AT EZRA'S RETURN as at Joshua's arrival (Arakhin 32b:10 — 30:5's 'your fathers possessed'), THE JUBILEE NULLIFIED when Reuben, Gad and half Manasseh were exiled — 'to all its inhabitants' (32b:15-17), the fiftieth counted to order the sabbaticals (32b:18; the arithmetic two arms 33a:1, Rosh Hashanah 9a:1)"), ('DATA', "the onset a PARAMETER (the_release_onset — after the conquest and the division; the count from the fourteenth year; renewed at Ezra's return); on the bare world before the entry the cell answers 'no count' — as the removal's date at 14:28; the exam's person the creditor in the wilderness — exempt from the release")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_territory) = ("the territory (15:2) — in the Land and outside it, 'because a release has been proclaimed to the LORD' (the Sifrei 112:11; Kiddushin 38b:1-4); when the jubilee is not in force the money's release stands by the Sages' decree (Gittin 36a:13-36b:1): THE PARAMETER the_release_territory; the creditor in Babylonia whose loan the seventh year passed barred from exacting", ['barred_from_it'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2 — "because a release has been proclaimed TO THE LORD" — the clause [\'Deut 15:2\'] (one seat); "to the LORD" in the chapter [2, 19, 21]'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 112:11 (read whole at the reading); Kiddushin 38b:1-4 (credited by address — Kiddushin 38b:3 the two releases at three seats); Gittin 36a:13-36b:1, Moed Katan 2b:17 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.cycle(50) = jubilee — IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE IT — 'because a release has been proclaimed to the LORD': in any case (112:11; Kiddushin 38b:1, 38b:4 the verse's own clause; Tosefta Kiddushin 1:10 the twin); WHEN THE JUBILEE IS NOT IN FORCE the money's release stands BY THE SAGES' DECREE in remembrance (Gittin 36a:13-36b:1 — Rabbi: 'this is the manner of the release: he shall release' speaks both releases; the debtor told to sit still, or the court's power over property 36b:3-4; Moed Katan 2b:17): THE TWO ARMS recorded — the Torah's release with the jubilee, the decree's without"), ('DATA', "the territory a PARAMETER (the_release_territory — in the Land and outside; the decree's arm when the jubilee is not in force); the exam's person the creditor in Babylonia whose loan the seventh year passed — released by the decree: barred from exacting")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_object) = ('the object (15:2) — loans only: not theft, deposit, wage or shop credit unless made standing debts (the Sifrei 112:5-7; Mishnah Sheviit 10:1-2; Tosefta Sheviit 8:5-7); what cannot yet be exacted not released (Makkot 3b:4): THE PARAMETER the_release_object; the shopkeeper whose credit was not made a loan accepted — his credit stands', ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2 — "every creditor shall release THE LOAN OF HIS HAND which he lends to his neighbor" — "the loan of his hand" [\'משה\', \'ידו\', \'ישה\'] (the creditor\'s verb\'s thirteen seats 13 — Exodus 22:24, the pledge 24:10-11, Elisha\'s widow, Nehemiah\'s usurers); Onkelos "the master of the claim"'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 112:5-7 (read whole at the reading); Mishnah Sheviit 10:1-2, Tosefta Sheviit 8:5-7 (read whole at the docket); Makkot 3b:4, Bava Batra 145b:2, Gittin 30a:16 (read whole at the docket) — LOANS ONLY — 'the loan of his hand': not a theft and a deposit (112:5), not a hireling's wage and the shop's credit (112:6) UNLESS MADE STANDING DEBTS (112:7 — 'as the loan of his hand is a standing debt, so all of them'); Mishnah Sheviit 10:1-2 the answer sheet: the shop's credit and the wage unless made loans, the fines and the court's obligations not released, the pledge-loan and the notes handed to the court not released; Tosefta 8:5-7 the shop split by Rabbi, the marriage contract, the lien (Gittin 37a:9-11 two arms); WHAT CANNOT YET BE EXACTED IS NOT RELEASED (Makkot 3b:4; Bava Batra 145b:2; the ten-year loan's two versions Makkot 3a:15 / 3b:4)"), ('DATA', "the object a PARAMETER (the_release_object — loans only; the exceptions' list from Sheviit 10:1-2 and Tosefta 8:5-7); the exam's person the shopkeeper whose credit was not made a loan — not released: accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_manner) = ("the manner (15:2) — 'and this is the manner of the release': the word 'I release it' (the Sifrei 112:1; Mishnah Sheviit 10:8 inside the spine); the creditor's eyes until 'nevertheless' (Gittin 37b:1-2); the oath released by the same word (Shevuot 49a:2): the debtor who pays anyway and says 'even so' accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2 — "AND THIS IS THE MANNER OF THE RELEASE" — "and this is the manner of" [\'1Kgs 9:15\', \'Deut 15:2\', \'Deut 19:4\'] (19:4\'s manslayer and Solomon\'s levy the kin); the infinitive absolute "release" [\'שמוט\'] at 15:2'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 112:1 (read whole at the reading); Mishnah Sheviit 10:8, Gittin 37b:1-2, Shabbat 148b:12, Shevuot 49a:2, Tosefta Sheviit 8:8 (read whole at the docket) — THE MANNER IS THE WORD — 'and this is the manner of the release': from here they said (Mishnah Sheviit 10:8) one who repays a debt in the seventh year, the creditor says to him 'I RELEASE IT'; if he said 'even so', he may accept it (112:1); the creditor may lift his eyes until 'nevertheless' (Gittin 37b:1-2); the edge of a loan made after the year (Shabbat 148b:12); THE OATH RELEASED BY THE SAME WORD (Shevuot 49a:2 — Mishnah Shevuot 7:8; Tosefta Sheviit 8:8 with R. Shimon's arm): THE FIVE SEATS of the manner"), ('DATA', 'the manner a DATA row (the_manner — the word said, Sheviit 10:8 inside the spine; the debtor who pays anyway thanked, the creditor\'s eyes until "nevertheless"); the exam\'s person the debtor who pays after the seventh year and hears "I release it" and says "even so" — accepted')])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_exaction) = ("the exaction (15:2) — 'he shall not exact' to put him under a prohibition (the Sifrei 112:8): THE WRITE exaction_barred, a BLOCK on Israel at the chapter's own day; the stipulation against the release void in its form, valid as the debtor's waiver (Makkot 3b:7-10): the creditor who exacts in the eighth year barred from it", ['exaction_barred'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2 — "HE SHALL NOT EXACT of his neighbor and his brother" — the negation [\'לא\'], "of his neighbor and his brother" [\'Deut 15:2\'] (one seat); the exaction verb\'s tokens [\'Deut 15:2\', \'Deut 15:3\', \'Exod 24:14\', \'Isa 50:8\', \'Isa 65:5\', \'Job 40:19\', \'Lev 21:21\', \'Lev 21:23\', \'Ps 91:7\'] (the lemma table collides — the tokens read); Onkelos "shall not claim"'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 112:8 (read whole at the reading); Makkot 3b:7-10 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_ordinances (CALL) — OR.loan(creditor_manner) = not_seen_at_all_times — 'HE SHALL NOT EXACT' — TO PUT HIM UNDER A PROHIBITION (112:8): the dunning creditor's negative command, THE BLOCK exaction_barred; Onkelos 'shall not claim' (the verb of the claim, not the approach — 22:24's 'as a creditor' the manner by CALL: not seen at all times); THE STIPULATION AGAINST THE RELEASE VOID IN ITS FORM, VALID AS THE DEBTOR'S WAIVER (Makkot 3b:7-10 — 'on condition that the seventh year not release it' void; 'that you not release it' valid); the creditor who exacts after the release transgresses — no act, no lashes"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE exaction_barred — a BLOCK on israel_people at the counter's day (DG2): the dunning after the release barred; the stipulation's two forms a DATA row; the exam's person the creditor who exacts in the eighth year — barred from it")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_two_exclusions_and_the_foreigner) = ("the two exclusions and the foreigner (15:2-3) — 'his neighbor' excludes others, 'his brother' the resident alien (the Sifrei 112:9-10); 'the foreigner you may exact' a positive command (113:1; yovel.interest_scope by CALL — the foreigner permitted, the brother barred, 23:21's twin): the creditor who exacts the foreigner after the seventh year accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2-3 — "his neighbor … his brother" the two nouns; "THE FOREIGNER you may exact" — "foreigner" in the book [(\'Deut 14:21\', \'לנכרי\'), (\'Deut 15:3\', \'הנכרי\'), (\'Deut 17:15\', \'נכרי\'), (\'Deut 23:21\', \'לנכרי\'), (\'Deut 29:21\', \'והנכרי\')] (14:21\'s carcass, this, 17:15\'s king, 23:21\'s interest, 29:21\'s visitor); "your brother" seven tokens in six verses {2: [\'אחיו\'], 3: [\'אחיך\'], 7: [\'אחיך\', \'מאחיך\'], 9: [\'באחיך\'], 11: [\'לאחיך\'], 12: [\'אחיך\']}; 23:21\'s twin [\'לנכרי\', \'תשיך\', \'ולאחיך\', \'לא\', \'תשיך\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 112:9-10, 113:1 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.interest_scope(foreigner) = permitted, (brother) = barred; cold_run_ordinances (CALL) — OR.loan(foreigner) = permitted — 'HIS NEIGHBOR' — TO THE EXCLUSION OF OTHERS (112:9: the foreigner outside the bar); 'HIS BROTHER' — to the exclusion of the resident alien (112:10); 'THE FOREIGNER YOU MAY EXACT' A POSITIVE COMMAND (113:1) — the same noun's rule at 23:21's interest ahead ('to the foreigner you may lend at interest, to your brother not' — yovel.interest_scope by CALL: the foreigner permitted, the brother barred); the release's two exclusions and the interest's the one pair"), ('DATA', "the two exclusions a DATA row (the_two_exclusions — the neighbor, the brother; the foreigner's exaction a positive command by the shelf, the interest's twin by CALL); the exam's person the creditor who exacts the foreigner after the seventh year — accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_two_years_powers) = ("the two years' powers (15:2) — the seventh year releases the loan, the jubilee frees the slave: two a fortiori arguments cancelled by two verses' 'this' (the Sifrei 112:2-4 — I1; Leviticus 25:13 by CALL to yovel.jubilee): the debtor who pleads the jubilee on his loan barred from it", ['barred_from_it'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2 — "and THIS is the manner of the release" — "this" [\'וזה\']; 15:12\'s "in the seventh year you shall send him away free" [\'ובשנה\', \'השביעת\', \'תשלחנו\', \'חפשי\']; Leviticus 25:10\'s "proclaim liberty" [\'Lev 25:10\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 112:2-4 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.jubilee() release_day = tenth_of_seventh_month_yom_kippur; YO.hebrew_slave(israelite, 60, 20, 6) exit = at_jubilee_with_children — THE TWO YEARS' POWERS — the release releases a loan and the jubilee does not (112:2); an a fortiori for the jubilee to release a loan REFUTED by 'and THIS is the manner of the release' (112:3 — I1, checked in MIDDOT.md: the seventh year alone); an a fortiori for the seventh year to free slaves REFUTED by 'in THIS year' (Leviticus 25:13 — 112:4): the jubilee frees the slave, the seventh year releases the loan — two a fortiori arguments cancelled by two verses' 'this'; Leviticus 25:13 by CALL to yovel.jubilee"), ('DATA', 'the two years\' powers a DATA row (the_two_years_powers — I1 twice, cancelled by "this" twice; the jubilee\'s liberty by CALL); the exam\'s person the debtor who pleads the jubilee on his loan — barred from it (the jubilee releases no loan)')])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_pledge_loan) = ("the pledge-loan (15:3) — 'what is yours with your brother your hand shall release', not what is your brother's in your hand (the Sifrei 113:2; Mishnah Sheviit 10:2 — the pledge-loan and the notes handed to the court not released; ordinances.loan by CALL for the pledge's own law): the creditor who holds a pledge after the seventh year accepted — the loan not released", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:3 — "and what is yours with your brother YOUR HAND SHALL RELEASE" — "your hand shall release" [\'Deut 15:3\'] (one seat); "your hand" in the chapter {2: [\'ידו\'], 3: [\'ידך\'], 7: [\'ידך\'], 8: [\'ידך\'], 10: [\'ידך\'], 11: [\'ידך\']}'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 113:2 (read whole at the reading); Mishnah Sheviit 10:2 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_ordinances (CALL) — OR.loan(pledge_sunset) = until_the_sun_sets, OR.loan(court_only) = only_through_the_court_outside_you_stand — THE PLEDGE-LOAN NOT RELEASED — 'what is yours with your brother your hand shall release': not what is your brother's in your hand (113:2 — the pledge held by the creditor); Mishnah Sheviit 10:2: one who lends on a pledge and one who hands his notes to the court — not released; the pledge's law by CALL (ordinances.loan — the garment returned by sunset, the court's entry only): the pledge held and the debt standing"), ('DATA', "the pledge-loan a DATA row (the_pledge_loan — not released, Sheviit 10:2; the pledge by CALL); the exam's person the creditor who holds a pledge for his loan after the seventh year — accepted, the loan not released")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_release(the_prozbul) = ("the prozbul (15:3) — 'your hand' and not the court's: the notes handed to the court not released (the Sifrei 113:3; Mishnah Sheviit 10:3-4 the writ's text; Gittin 36a:11-37b:8 — Hillel's reason 15:9, the ground rabbinic against rabbinic, the land condition, the presumption): THE PARAMETER the_prozbul, a procedure not code; the lender with a prozbul who collects after the seventh year accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:3 — "your hand shall release" — YOUR hand, not the court\'s: the possessive on "hand" [\'ידך\']; the chapter\'s "hand" six tokens 6'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 113:3 (read whole at the reading); Mishnah Sheviit 10:3-4, 10:6 (inside the spine and at the docket); Gittin 36a:11-37b:8, Tosefta Sheviit 8:9-11, Makkot 3b (read whole at the docket) — HILLEL'S PROZBUL (the court's writ) A PARAMETER FROM THE ANSWER SHEET — 'your hand' and not the court's: one who hands his notes to the court is not released (113:3 — the verse leaves the procedure open; Mishnah Sheviit 10:3-4 THE TEXT 'I hand over to you, the judges in such a place, that any debt I have I may collect whenever I wish', the judges or the witnesses sign); Gittin 36a:11-13 THE REASON the verse's own warning (15:9) and THE GROUND rabbinic against rabbinic — the release in Hillel's day rabbinic; the land condition and its minimum, the substitutes and the perforated pot (Mishnah 10:6; Gittin 37a:3-7; Tosefta 8:10), the writ by speech (37a:6), the date (Tosefta 8:11), the orphans' exemption (37a:2), THE PRESUMPTION 'I had one and lost it' a dispute (37b:5-8), the scope for all generations (36b:5-10 — Shmuel 'I will nullify it', Rav Nachman 'I will uphold it'); the witnesses Makkot 3b: A PROCEDURE, NOT CODE"), ('DATA', "THE PROZBUL A PARAMETER (the_prozbul — the writ's text from Sheviit 10:4; the reason, the ground, the land condition, the presumption; a procedure the verse leaves open); the exam's person the lender with a prozbul who collects after the seventh year — accepted")])
DATA KEYS release_firstborn ~ end|year|release|calendar|onset|hakhel|31|swore: ['the_release_date', 'the_firstlings_year', 'the_release_onset', 'the_release_territory', 'the_release_object', 'the_one_calendar', 'the_two_years_powers', 'lend_not_borrow', 'the_lending_obligation', 'the_six_years_by_the_clock', 'the_three_sendings', 'the_tending_term']
CELL food_tithe.the_third_year: asks 14 ['one_tithe_not_two', 'the_levite_never_interrupted', 'the_removal_date', 'the_seventh_year_by_the_cycle', 'the_tithes_new_year', 'the_gifts_exempt', 'the_four_in_want', 'the_measures', 'the_uses_barred', 'the_convert_at_the_gate', 'the_resident_alien_at_the_gate', 'ezras_penalty', 'the_courtyard_from_your_gates', 'the_animal_tithe_now'] | keys 0 []
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_removal_date) = ("the removal's date (14:28) — the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; the Sifrei 109:1-3 — I2 with 31:10): THE PARAMETER the_removal_date, the date the calendar's own key; the one who removes the tithes on that eve accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28 — "at the END of three years" — "at the end" in the book [\'Deut 13:8\', \'Deut 14:28\', \'Deut 15:1\', \'Deut 28:49\', \'Deut 28:64\', \'Deut 31:10\', \'Deut 9:11\'] (15:1, 31:10 the seven years\' twins: "at the end of seven years" [\'Deut 15:1\', \'Deut 31:10\', \'Jer 34:14\'])'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:1-3 (read whole at the reading — I2 with 31:10, checked in MIDDOT.md); Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(removal) = the removal on Passover eve of the fourth and seventh years — the firs; the parameter the_removal_date = ['one_tithe_not_two', 'the_eve', 'the_uses', 'the_years']; the calendar's keys passover_1 {'month': 1, 'day': 15}, passover_7 {'from': 'passover_1', 'plus': 6} — THE REMOVAL'S DATE A CLOCK DATUM — 'at the end of three years' read with 31:10's 'at the end of seven years, at the festival' (I2): the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year the time of removal (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; 109:1-3); KO.the_tithe 'removal' the first tithe's side; the date rendered by the calendar's own keys (passover_7's eve), never a constant; 26:12 ahead the confession's seat"), ('DATA', "THE PARAMETER the_removal_date on file (DF6 — ['one_tithe_not_two', 'the_eve', 'the_uses', 'the_years']; the eve's key passover_7 the calendar's); the exam's person the one who removes the tithes on the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth year — accepted")])
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(one_tithe_not_two) = ("one tithe not two (14:28) — the poor man's tithe replaces the second in the third and the sixth year (the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5), the Levite never interrupted (KO.the_tithe by CALL): THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a STATUS on Israel at the chapter's own day; the readback row 14:28 SUPPLIED AS A LAW with its write", ['poor_tithe_owed'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28 — "AT THE END OF THREE YEARS you shall bring out all the tithe of your yield in that year" — "at the end of three years" [\'2Kgs 18:10\', \'Deut 14:28\'] (2 Kings 18:10 Samaria\'s fall the one kin); the parser\'s [3] [3] and the starred token [\'שנים*\', \'מעשר*\']; "the tithe of your yield" [\'Deut 14:28\', \'Deut 26:12\'] (14:28, 26:12)'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11 (read whole at the reading); Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(third_year) = the first tithe every year — juxtaposed to an inheritance (R; the tape (the recon): portion_declared at Num 18:20 — ONE TITHE NOT TWO — in the third and the sixth year the poor man's tithe REPLACES the second (109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-2 — the second year into the third, 'the year of THE tithe'); THE LEVITE NEVER INTERRUPTED — the first tithe every year: R. Yehuda from 14:29's Levite, R. Eliezer ben Yaakov from the inheritance's juxtaposition (12b:4-5; KO.the_tithe 'third_year' by CALL — already a move there)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a NEW STATUS on israel_people at the counter's day (40, 11, 1) (DF2, DF4; the one database on Israel []); the readback row 14:28 SUPPLIED AS A LAW WITH THE WRITE (the kin by CALL — yovel, korach); the Levite's first tithe unmoved")])
